NegroniMetal change to ios-flame 745c434 phone/metal2 (on top of flame/0001-0014), applied by scripts/metal/fetch-sources.sh:
the render-pass pieces WebKit's ANGLE Metal back end (20H392 libANGLE-shared.dylib) uses for WebGL, missing before
(docs/metal-webgl-2026-10-27.md; found with scripts/metal/angleprobe.sh and the Safari GPU process log):
1. Bridge (NativeMetalObjects.h/.rs): NmbPassAttachment carries the multisample resolve target (resolve_texture/_level/_slice/
   _depth_plane -> the runtime's resolve_* fields; before: dropped, so ANGLE's MSAA framebuffer pass was refused as
   RenderPass(ResolveWithoutTexture(Depth))), and three late store-action calls nmb_render_set_{color,depth,stencil}_store_action
   over the runtime's set_*_store_action (ANGLE begins every pass with MTLStoreActionUnknown and decides at endEncoding).
   The struct grows at the end (repr(C) on both sides); bridge and plugin are built from the same tree.
2. Frontend: the pass attachment lambda passes the resolve texture (retained with the pass, IOSurface resolve targets counted as
   written); NBRenderEncoder gets setColorStoreAction:atIndex:, setDepthStoreAction:, setStencilStoreAction: (the *Options: forms
   are no-ops), the ...SamplerStates:withRange: forms and the LOD-clamp forms ...SamplerState:lodMinClamp:lodMaxClamp:atIndex: /
   ...SamplerStates:lodMinClamps:lodMaxClamps:withRange: on the render and compute encoders. ANGLE binds every sampler with the
   LOD-clamp form (mtl::RenderCommandEncoder::endEncodingImpl replays it): the unimplemented selector was an
   NSInvalidArgumentException that ended com.apple.WebKit.GPU (metal.log `MISSING NBRenderEncoder
   -setFragmentSamplerState:lodMinClamp:lodMaxClamp:atIndex:`). The clamps are not in the bridge (the sampler's own lod_min/lod_max
   are used); a narrowing clamp is logged once.

